UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-art-program-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Art Program
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Art Program scheme contributes to the cos
 ts of an art programme: a series of activities (exhibitions\, presentation
 s\, lectures\, workshops\, etc.) with an artistic\, substantive\, thematic
  and/or formal connection that take place within a certain period. It also
  covers exchange activities with other countries and programmes for guest 
 studios and artist-in-residencies.\n\nOrganisation: Stroom Den Haag\nLocat
 ion: The Hague\, Netherlands. Aimed at non-profit organisations\, artist i
 nitiatives\, collectives and independent curators/organisers\; applicants 
 from outside The Hague apply with a CV\, provided the programme benefits T
 he Hague's art climate.\nAward: Maximum EUR 10\,000 per application\, up t
 o EUR 20\,000 per applicant per calendar year. Requests above EUR 5\,000 r
 equire at least 30 percent co-financing of the total budget from third par
 ties. Compliance with the kunstenaarshonorarium.nl artist fee guideline is
  part of the assessment. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; th
 e grant remains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, wit
 h 80 percent paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: http
 s://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-program?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-p
 rogram?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Aimed at non-profit organisations\, artis
 t initiatives\, collectives and independent curators/organisers\; applican
 ts from outside The Hague apply with a CV\, provided the programme benefit
 s The Hague's art climate.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brooks-international-fellowship-tate-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Brooks International Fellowship Programme 2027 (Tate Brit
 ain x Delfina Foundation)
DESCRIPTION:Tate\, in collaboration with Delfina Foundation\, invites appli
 cations for the thirteenth Brooks International Fellowship Programme: two 
 6-month fellowships in 2027 for international researchers based outside th
 e UK\, hosted in the Tate Britain Curatorial Division and complemented by 
 activities and residency life at Delfina Foundation.\n\nOrganisation: Tate
 \, in collaboration with Delfina Foundation\nLocation: London\, UK (workin
 g at Tate Britain\, living at Delfina Foundation). Open to international r
 esearchers based outside the UK.\nAward: Fully funded 6-month fellowship: 
 living allowance bursary of GBP 40 per day\, single bedroom at Delfina Fou
 ndation (house of up to 8 residents with shared facilities)\, return econo
 my flight\, UK airport transfers\, visa fee reimbursement with visa suppor
 t\, London Underground and bus travel pass\, a research resource allowance
 \, and travel to other Tate galleries (Tate Modern\, Liverpool\, St Ives) 
 and other UK and European cultural institutions. Two fellowships available
 . No application fee.\nDuration: Six months\, 5 April to 17 September 2027
 \n\nMore: https://jobsearch.tate.org.uk/jobs/job/Brooks-International-Fell
 ow-Programme/839?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://jobsearch.tate.org.uk/jobs/job/Brooks-International-Fellow-Prog
 ramme/839?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:London\, UK (working at Tate Britain\, living at Delfina Foundatio
 n). Open to international researchers based outside the UK.
END:VEVENT
